        "collapse_whitespace"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    "explanation": "01010111 = 87 = W; 01001001 = 73 = I; 01001110 = 78 = N."
   },
   {
    "label": "(f)",
    "type": "SHORT_ANSWER",
    "marks": 2,
    "markingMode": "MANUAL",
    "stem": "The club wants to send messages that include emojis. Explain why ASCII cannot be used and what should be used instead.",
    "answerSpec": {
     "markScheme": {
      "points": [
       {
        "id": "p1",
        "description": "ASCII uses 7 (or 8) bits, so it has only 128 (or 256) codes, none of which are emojis.",
        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p2",
        "description": "Unicode should be used: it uses more bits per character, so it has codes for emojis and characters of many languages.",
        "marks": 1
       }
      ]
     },
     "markingNotes": "Example answer: ASCII only has 128 characters (256 in extended ASCII), and emojis are not among them. Unicode uses more bits per character, giving enough codes for emojis and other languages."
    }
   }
  ],
  "explanation": "(a) 10010011. (b) 01100101 = 101. (d) 01010010. (e) WIN.",
